 State←InitialState object;t;color;fontobj;fontdef;px;props;newpic
⍝ Create a base starting state from default values derived from the target object

 State←() ⍝ Build us a namespace to begin tracking the command's drawing states as we go
 State._class←'(State)'
 State._Class←object._Class ⍝ Just to keep some things from crashing
 State._Owner←object ⍝ To allow some objects to be created as the parent's children
⍝? Let's assume here that EVERY Draw command will require a Bitmap for drawing; Create one if necessary
 :If 0=object.⎕NC'_pic'
⍝? This will not work! Only Printer and Root have DevCaps, so we'll need another method to handle other controls (Picture & Printer already have this)
     ##.Halt'This will not function if object does not already have a _pic Bitmap'
     px←⊃object ##.∆WG'DevCaps'
     props←⊂'Bitmap'
     props,←⊂'CBits'(px⍴¯1+⌊256*3) ⍝ Start with a completely white paper
     newpic←⎕VGET(object⍕⍛,'._pic')##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the hidden Dyalog object to hold the dynamic image
     ##.New.InitChild object newpic
 :EndIf
 State.target←object._pic ⍝ Now we're going to do all our Draw operations directly on this Bitmap ⍝? (Might get rid of this variable later and use a ._pic constant)
 State.(_size _extent)←object.(_size _extent)
 State._Ancestry←object,object._Ancestry ⍝ Only for utility support (might need _Owner for other things?)
 State._pix_size←object._pix_size
 :If 2=object.⎕NC'_units' ⋄ State._units←object._units ⋄ :EndIf
 ⍝State.NewName←~'Picture' 'Printer'∊⍨⊂object._class ⍝ Drawing on non-Picture-ish controls requires naming graphical objects ⍝? Will we dispense with this altogether and always use _pic?
 State.NewName←0 ⍝? We won't use permanent names anywhere for now, but keep the flag around in case we change our minds later
 State._dirty←0 ⍝ Keep track of this locally so we only need to set it once per Draw

 color←3⍴¨255 0 ⍝? Make sure that no colors are ever defaulted! (Always assume Black on White to start)
 ⍝color←object ⎕VGET⊂'_color_'(¯1 ¯1) ⍝ Obtain target's already-defined colors
 ⍝:If ∨/t←¯1∊¨color ⋄ (t/color)←object ##.Classes._supp.color0 t/color ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Follow color inheritence
 {}State ##.Classes.color color ⍝ Assign these to our standard internal values for later use

 ⍝ The State is going to contain object names in variables rather than object references or properties: FontObj, IconObj, BrushBmp
 fontdef←State ⎕VGET⊂'_font'('MS Shell Dlg' 1 0 'ansi') ⍝ What font is defined on the parent object - capture it for a duplicate construction
 {}State(##.Classes.font ChangeError'font' 'Font')fontdef ⍝ Call the system font-creation path but put resulting object name in State.FontObj
 fontobj←State ⎕VGET⊂'FontObj' '' ⍝? This better only be a object name, now
 'Internal problems creating a default Draw font'##.Error 0=≢fontobj
 State.IconObj←State.BrushBmp←'' ⍝ Default to none used yet

 State._scale←object ⎕VGET⊂'_scale' 1
 State._pen←1(2⊃color)1 ⍝ Default to foreground color
 State._brush←1(1⊃color) ⍝ Default to background color
 State._mode←object ⎕VGET⊂'_mode'(1 13 0)
 State.Window←State.Clip←⍬ ⍝ Default to no Windowing/Clipping
 State.Window_Mask←State.Clip_Mask←0 0⍴0 ⍝ These will be boolean matrices when used
